[**List of newspapers held in the State Archive of East Kazakhstan Region for 1935–2011, as of 1 January 2018**](old/akimsemey/other/%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%8B%20%D0%B7%D0%B0%201935-2017.docx)

**[Fonds of the State Archive of East Kazakhstan Region as of 1 January 2018](old/akimsemey/other/%D0%A4%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%8B%20%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%85%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B0%20%D0%92%D0%9A%D0%9E%20%D0%BD%D0%B0%202018%D0%B3..xlsb)**

**[Party fonds of the State Archive of East Kazakhstan Region as of 1 January 2018](old/akimsemey/other/%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%82%20%D1%84%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%8B%20%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%85%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B0%20%D0%92%D0%9A%D0%9E%20%D0%BD%D0%B0%202018%D0%B3..xlsb)**

The State Archive of East Kazakhstan Region holds documents reflecting the period when Soviet power was established in the city: the Ust-Kamenogorsk district revolutionary committee, the district executive committee, the district military commissariat, special-purpose units and district institutions.

Of particular value are the fonds whose documents reflect the development of industry, since East Kazakhstan is a region with well-developed mining, metallurgical and machine-building industries. These are the fonds of the East Kazakhstan Council of the National Economy (Sovnarkhoz); the Belogorsk mining and processing, Irtysh polymetallic, and Ust-Kamenogorsk lead-zinc and titanium-magnesium plants; the valve, machine-building and capacitor factories; the Ust-Kamenogorsk “Gidrostalkonstruktsiya” plant and the instrument-making plant. Local, light and food industries are also well developed in our region. The archive holds documents of the Ust-Kamenogorsk silk fabrics mill, the “Rassvet” factory, the Ust-Kamenogorsk meat-processing plant, the oil mill, the dairy plant, the joint-stock company “Ust-Kamenogorsk Khleboprodukt” and others. East Kazakhstan has immense mineral wealth. The fonds of the East Kazakhstan Geological Department and its expeditions contain rich material on mineral resources, survey methods, and the geological characteristics of East Kazakhstan Region. Another feature of the Rudny Altai is its abundant energy resources. The archive holds the fonds of the district “Altaienergo” administration, the Ust-Kamenogorsk hydroelectric power station, and the “Irtyshgesstroy” construction department for hydroelectric power stations on the Irtysh.

The archive's fonds preserve documents of the East Kazakhstan Regional Council of People's Deputies and its executive committee, the offices of the Akims of East Kazakhstan Region and of the city of Ust-Kamenogorsk, the Ust-Kamenogorsk City Council of People's Deputies and its executive committee, the East Kazakhstan regional and city maslikhats, documents of district executive committees and district akims, as well as of the East Kazakhstan regional party committee, the regional Komsomol committee, city and district party and Komsomol committees, and institutions of education, health care, culture, communications, transport, housing and utilities, state property, taxation, economy and finance. The history of agriculture is reflected in the fonds of regional and district agricultural institutions.

East Kazakhstan is one of the few regions of our country with large stands of industrial timber. The fonds of the regional forestry department, forestry enterprises and the “Kazles” logging and woodworking trust are therefore of great interest.

Industrial, housing and cultural-welfare construction is described in the documents of construction trusts and construction and assembly departments, the largest of which are “Altaisvinetsstroy” and the “Irtysh Construction Department”.

The fonds of scientific and design institutions contain, besides administrative records, scientific and technical documentation. These are the fonds of the All-Union Research Institute of Non-Ferrous Metals “VNIItsvetmet”, the state design institute “Kazgiprotsvetmet”, the Ust-Kamenogorsk branch of the Kazakh state institute for the design of water-management structures “Kazgiprovodkhoz” (Order of the Badge of Honour), the “Keramika” plant, the joint-stock company “Irtysh Chemical and Metallurgical Plant”, the state design institute for housing and civil construction “Vostokgrazhdanproekt”, the state open joint-stock company “Belogorsk Mining and Processing Plant” and others.

Of definite interest are the collections of documents on the history of East Kazakhstan: “The development of virgin and fallow lands in East Kazakhstan Region”, “The partisan movement in East Kazakhstan”, a collection of documents on land management of farms in East Kazakhstan Region, on the history of sport in East Kazakhstan Region, “The movement for communist labour”, “East Kazakhstan in the years of the Great Patriotic War, 1941–1945”, memoirs of war and labour veterans, and a collection of documents found in foreign archives and scientific institutions on the history of the region, and others.

Our region is renowned for its eminent scientists, figures of science, culture and the arts, writers, and public and political figures. Their documents are of enormous historical and scientific-practical importance.

The regional state archive holds 76 fonds of personal origin.

Among the fonds' creators are:
- I. V. Berdus, Honoured Power Engineer of the Kazakh SSR and director of the Leninogorsk cascade of hydroelectric power stations;
- A. M. Volkov, a well-known writer, scholar and teacher;
- B. G. Gerasimov, a well-known local historian and scholar, founder of the Semipalatinsk sub-department of the Russian Geographical Society;
- N. Ya. Konshin, a political exile of the Narodnaya Volya movement, local historian, founder of the Semipalatinsk sub-department of the West Siberian Department of the Russian Geographical Society;
- I. I. Kotov, a Lenin Prize laureate, mechanic and inventor;
- P. N. Kuznetsov, a writer and journalist, translator of the works of the Kazakh akyn Zhambyl;
- the Pankratyevs, well-known gardeners and local historians;
- N. S. Pakhotina, Doctor of Medical Sciences;
- S. A. Amanzholov, Doctor of Philology, professor, corresponding member of the Academy of Sciences of Kazakhstan, an outstanding linguist and Turkologist;
- U. B. Maldybayev, head of the regional department of culture, a participant in the Great Patriotic War;
- N. A. Petrovsky, a self-taught scholar, author of the Dictionary of Russian Personal Names;
- K. K. Zhamanbayev, Honoured Teacher of the Kazakh SSR;
- S. E. Chernykh, Excellent Worker of Archival Affairs of the USSR, writer, local historian, Honoured Worker of Culture of the Kazakh SSR;
- A. V. Yegorina, Doctor of Geographical Sciences, professor;
- V. A. Rybakov, a collector of Russian surnames;
- P. S. Tikhonovskaya, Excellent Worker of Public Education;
- the Belosludov brothers, scholars and local historians;
- O. Bokeyev, a playwright and State Prize laureate of Kazakhstan;
- M. V. Gorokhov, a local historian and photojournalist of the newspapers “Priirtyshsky Kommunar” and “Omskaya Pravda”;
- M. M. Kagarmanova, a representative of the Tatar diaspora in Ust-Kamenogorsk;
- V. E. Murygin and N. S. Rakhvalov, participants in the struggle to establish Soviet power in East Kazakhstan;
- K. Sakabayev, a journalist, writer and member of the Writers' Union of Kazakhstan;
- Ye. K. Turlybayev, Excellent Worker of Public Education of the Kazakh SSR, journalist;
- Yu. K. Uvaliyev, a teacher, scholar, honorary professor of East Kazakhstan State University;
- N. V. Alekseyenko, a teacher, Doctor of Historical Sciences, professor, Honorary Citizen of Ust-Kamenogorsk;
- Ya. Ya. Yaunrodzin, editor of the newspapers of the political department of the Ukrainian MTS “Udarnik Kolkhoznykh Polei” and of the Kirov district party committee and district executive committee “Priirtyshsky Kommunar”;
- the Popovs, candidates of geographical sciences and teachers;
- M. Sh. Musin, a member of the USSR Union of Journalists, editor-in-chief of the literary magazine “Vostok”, correspondent of Radio Liberty, a participant in the Great Patriotic War;
- Turgazy Nukayuly, a poet, writer, member of the Writers' Union of Kazakhstan, first deputy editor of the newspaper “Didar”, local historian;
- Serik Gabdullauly Gabdulin, a poet, journalist, member of the Writers' Union of Kazakhstan, the first head of the “Kazakh Tili” society, editor-in-chief of the republican literary magazine “Ak Ertis”;
- G. N. Pussep, director of the public foundation of Honorary Citizens of Ust-Kamenogorsk “My City”, member of the Union of Journalists of Kazakhstan and of the association of the creative intelligentsia of East Kazakhstan Region;
- Nikandr Aleksandrovich Petrovsky, a self-taught scholar, a leading specialist in onomastics, author of the “Dictionary of Russian Personal Names”;
- Nikolai Nikiforovich Yakovlev, Doctor of Historical Sciences, professor, organiser of the State Public Historical Library in Moscow, a leading specialist in the history of the first Russian revolution;
- Kirill Flavianovich Yermolayev, Candidate of Geological and Mineralogical Sciences, head of the analytical geology sector of the Altai Department of the K. I. Satpayev Institute of Geological Sciences of the Academy of Sciences of the Kazakh SSR;
- Aldiyar Akylbekovich Aubakirov (born 20.01.1949), an amateur poet, collector, head of the East Kazakhstan regional archives administration;
- Zh. Ch. Zhangozin, director and editor-in-chief of the Ulan district newspaper “Ulan Tany” (“Ulan Dawns”), member of the USSR Union of Journalists and of the Union of Journalists of Kazakhstan, Excellent Worker of the Information Industry, figure of culture of Kazakhstan, Honorary Citizen of Ulan District, and many others.

The documents of personal fonds held by the regional state archive are an invaluable source and are often used in preparing exhibitions, school lessons, lectures, creative evenings and documentary films.

The State Archive holds a historically unique layer of documents of regional, city, district and volost party committees of the Communist Party of Kazakhstan and of the Leninist Young Communist League of Kazakhstan, revealing the political and socio-economic history of the Kazakh SSR under the leadership of the CPSU.

The archive holds not only paper documents but also audiovisual ones. There are 7,839 storage units. They include photographs of the surroundings of pre-revolutionary and present-day Ust-Kamenogorsk; photographs of famous people; photographs and films of notable events in our city and region; sound recordings; and films about the development of non-ferrous metallurgy: “On the creative cooperation of the TMK, reconstruction of workshop No. 3”; “Brigade contracting in underground mines. The Belousovsky mine”; “50 years of the Leninogorsk mine”; “His name is titanium. A story about the work of smelters at the Ust-Kamenogorsk titanium-magnesium plant”; reports on the work of the open-pit and underground workings of the Tishinsky mine of the Leninogorsk polymetallic plant, and more.

As of 1 January 2020 the State Archive of East Kazakhstan Region holds **1,005 fonds – 610,492 storage units**.
